Aim: To practice source code management by uploading the User Registration application developed in Experiment 1 to GitHub.

Requirements:
- Git
- GitHub account
- User Registration Java project
Procedure
Step 1: Create a repository on GitHub
1. Open GitHub.
2. Login to your account.
3. Click on New Repository.
4. Enter repository name as UserRegistration.
5. Select Public.
6. Click Create Repository.
Step 2: Open the project folder in terminal
cd UserRegistration


Step 3: Initialize Git
git init


Step 4: Check the files
git status


Step 5: Add all source code files
git add .


Step 6: Commit the files
git commit -m "Initial commit - User Registration"


Step 7: Connect the local repository to GitHub
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/UserRegistration.git


Replace username with your GitHub username.

Step 8: Push the code to GitHub
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main


Expected output
Enumerating objects
Counting objects
Writing objects
To https://github.com/username/UserRegistration.git
 * [new branch] main -> main


Step 9: Modify the source code
Make a small change in UserController.java, such as changing:
return "Registration Successful!";


to:
return "User Registered Successfully!";


Save the file.
Step 10: Update GitHub
git status
git add .
git commit -m "Updated registration message"
git push origin main


Step 11: Verify
Open your GitHub repository and refresh the page.

You can see:
- Uploaded Java source code.
- Updated files.
- Commit history.
- Changes made to the project.
Result: Successfully practiced source code management by uploading, modifying, committing, and pushing the User Registration application to GitHub.
